From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonid <leonidy.1985@yandex.ru>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:35:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: t1100: nest the OTG vbus regulator inside the
 charger node

The mt6370 charger driver registers its OTG boost regulator with
of_match = "usb-otg-vbus-regulator" and no explicit of_node, so the
regulator core resolves it against the charger device node children
(regulator_of_get_init_node). The upstream mt6370-charger binding also
defines usb-otg-vbus-regulator as a child of the charger node.

We had it as a sibling of charger (both children of the mt6370 MFD
node), so the lookup never matched, the regulator registered with
of_node = NULL, and mtu3 could not resolve vbus-supply = <&mt6370_otg_vbus>:
"failed to get vbus" -> -EPROBE_DEFER forever -> no UDC, no USB gadget.

Move the node inside charger. The phandle stays global, so the ssusb
and tcpc vbus-supply references are unchanged. Verified on hardware:
mtu3 probes, UDC 11201000.usb reaches "configured", RNDIS gadget comes up.
---
 .../boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts  | 26 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
index 44cdb40fc..8afbdd95e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
@@ -375,14 +375,26 @@ charger {
 				      <&mt6370_adc MT6370_CHAN_TS_BAT>,
 				      <&mt6370_adc MT6370_CHAN_IBUS>,
 				      <&mt6370_adc MT6370_CHAN_IBAT>;
-		};
 
-		mt6370_otg_vbus: usb-otg-vbus-regulator {
-			regulator-name = "mt6370-usb-otg-vbus";
-			regulator-min-microvolt = <4350000>;
-			regulator-max-microvolt = <5800000>;
-			regulator-min-microamp = <500000>;
-			regulator-max-microamp = <3000000>;
+			/*
+			 * The OTG boost regulator must be a child of the
+			 * charger node, not a sibling: mt6370_chg_otg_rdesc
+			 * .of_match = "usb-otg-vbus-regulator" is resolved by
+			 * regulator_of_get_init_node() against the charger
+			 * device's of_node children. As a sibling it was never
+			 * found, the regulator registered with of_node=NULL and
+			 * mtu3's vbus-supply = <&mt6370_otg_vbus> phandle could
+			 * not resolve -> "failed to get vbus", probe deferred
+			 * forever, no UDC and no USB gadget. The phandle stays
+			 * global, so &ssusb and &tcpc references are unchanged.
+			 */
+			mt6370_otg_vbus: usb-otg-vbus-regulator {
+				regulator-name = "mt6370-usb-otg-vbus";
+				regulator-min-microvolt = <4350000>;
+				regulator-max-microvolt = <5800000>;
+				regulator-min-microamp = <500000>;
+				regulator-max-microamp = <3000000>;
+			};
 		};
 
 		/*
